FIGURE's patch 2 of 2 to ImGuiColorTextEdit (goossens fork, commit 9f812a0 (2026-11-13)).

TextEditor::cursorWidth has no initial value. TextEditor::render calls updateState (TextEditor.cpp:145, 150) before
it sets cursorWidth (:168-170), and updateState adds cursorWidth to the editor's total width (:1203-1210). So a fresh
editor's first frame computes its content size from whatever the heap held; at the second frame Dear ImGui truncates
it to an int (ImTrunc in SetNextWindowContentSize), and a huge or NaN value is IEEE invalid: a SIGFPE under traps
(found by xall_figure's GUI tests, gfortran -ffpe-trap=invalid, intermittently). The member gets the value render
gives it without a style (1 pixel at scale 1). Applied to third_party/ImGuiColorTextEdit/TextEditor.h; checked by
src/tests/figure_test_editor.F90 (check 15: a fresh editor drawn twice under traps, its heap filled with 0x7F bytes,
in a child process). To report upstream.

--- a/TextEditor.h
+++ b/TextEditor.h
@@ -2096,1 +2096,1 @@
-	float cursorWidth;
+	float cursorWidth = 1.0f;
